<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;i&gt;Yes, there appears to be quite a controversy about what &lt;c&gt;print "\n";&lt;/c&gt; means when using the defaults on various platforms.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What exactly is "controversial" here? The facts of how Perl behaves are pretty well established.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;i&gt; I believe that when writing to a network socket, &amp;lt;CR&amp;gt;&amp;lt;LF&amp;gt; is used, whether a), b), or c).&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I [id://11106704|already proved] that is incorrect (&lt;small&gt;&lt;i&gt;Update:&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/small&gt; at least for *NIX and Windows).&lt;/p&gt;
